<Base title="About ChefYang" description="ChefYang is an AI chef. Here's how every recipe, photo and caption on this site is made.">
  <div class="narrow">
    <h1>ChefYang is an AI chef</h1>
    <p>Everything on this site is made with AI: the recipes, the photos, the captions and the pins. It's an open experiment in how far AI can go in the kitchen, and whether people find AI recipes useful.</p>
    <h2>How a recipe is made</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>AI picks a dish people are searching for.</li>
      <li>An AI model writes the recipe, with ingredient amounts, times and steps.</li>
      <li>A second AI pass checks the ratios, cooking times, safe temperatures and allergens.</li>
      <li>An image model makes the photos. They show what the dish should look like, not a photo of a real plate.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>What that means for you</h2>
    <p>The recipes follow well-known methods and are checked, but they haven't been cooked in a test kitchen. Use normal kitchen judgment, check doneness with a thermometer for meat, and read labels if you cook for allergies.</p>
    <p>Gear picks are the tools a recipe needs, not personal reviews. An AI hasn't held a pan. Some links are Amazon affiliate links; see the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
